     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those admin rights need a foothold on the same host, and each foothold needs stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those in turn need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, and the only ways to get them are auth_dc and auth_adfs. Both require NOT mfa_admin, and the deployed mfa:admin defence makes mfa_admin true, so both are blocked. The attacker can still get a foothold, pivot internally, compromise the app and API servers, and obtain stolen_admin via kerberoasting. However, there is no path to stolen_dbadmin, so exfiltrated cannot be reached.\"}"
    }
   ],
